### 6a. Transaction Proxy cannot accept ATICA over HTTP (defect found 2026-08-19, blocks EPP-12266)
Every `POST /Cards/Transactions/process` with an ATICA body returns 500. TPS logs: `ATICAToTDEMappingStep` → `MappingRefusedException: busAppl <- TxChrtcs.AddtlData[.Tp=BUAI].Val … getTxChrtcs() is null`. Source: the ingress DTO `TransactionProxyRequest` is generated from `transaction-proxy-openapi.json` whose schema is a legacy shape (`account1`, `acquirer`, `actionCode`, …); `TransactionServiceImpl` does `objectMapper.convertValue(dto, ATICAMessageRoot.class)` ("both have same schema structure" — they do not), so ATICA blocks such as `TxChrtcs` are dropped before mapping and the one hard-required mapper target refuses. Adding `TxChrtcs` to the request changes nothing. **Nothing in the repo posts a working transaction to TPS** (`testing-tools/send_transaction.sh` has no sample body; `tps-e2e` is empty). **Fix built (Aug 19, branch `feature/tps-accept-atica-ingress`, `b0a9bc8f1`, 13 files +642/−55, TPS suite 50 tests green, spotless green):** (i) `RequestBodyCachingFilter` (OncePerRequestFilter + ContentCachingRequestWrapper, POST only) caches the wire body; the controller keeps the generated `TransactionProxyApi` signature (contract, bean validation, springdoc untouched) and hands the service the raw ATICA JSON; `TransactionService.processTransaction(String aticaJson, headers)`; `convertValue` removed, payload enters the workflow as JSON_STRING so `SchemaValidationStep` validates the real document. (ii) Second defect found on the way: `aticaObjectReader` bean used the default getter-based `JsonObjectMapper`, which derives lowerCamelCase names (`txChrtcs`, `pan`) and silently ignores the ISO UpperCamelCase wire keys — host-adapter/RTFA/NRTFA/TDS all use `JsonObjectMapper.avroFieldAccess()`, TPS was the exception; switched. Without (ii) the smoke would still fail with the same refusal. Tests: MockMvc + filter (body verbatim, `Card.PAN` and `TxChrtcs.AddtlData[BUAI]=BA` deserialised; 400 on missing `messageTypeId` / bad JSON), embedded Tomcat with the real filter chain, step+reader test handing the mapper an ATICAMessageRoot with BUAI/BA. Not done: (a) regenerate DTO from ATICA canonical would need api-spec/picker-profile rework (TPS api-spec sources `transactionProxyRequest` from `message-schema-package-legacy` canonical_universal_transaction.json via a governed picker profile) — follow-up; (b) `additionalProperties:true` is a dead end (openapi-generator 6.6.0 JavaSpring pojo.mustache emits no `@JsonAnySetter`). Proposal for the TPS owner; needs a defect ticket (no create rights). Until then the proxy E2E and the smoke round-trip cannot pass; the `tde-injector-simulator` path (`/inject`, returns `statusCode`) is the only way to push a transaction into TDS→TLRS→TIS in cards-devops and needs its own request shape worked out.

