## 7a. Captured effective status (TLS read-time derivation) — **Jira: EPP-15771** "Cards - Integration APIs - Universal Transaction Service - Bug - Captured Transactions - Init/Enabled Status in Retrieve" (Raluca assigned it to Narendra 2026-08-28 13:25 UTC and moved it Open → In Progress at 13:30; lives on **Jira Cloud `aciworldwide1.atlassian.net`, project "Payment Hub" / EPP** — see §2) — PR #1108, verified against real services 2026-08-25, correlation proof pending the smoke round trip

Story: "Derive Captured Transaction Effective Status from Authorized Transaction During Retrieval" (= EPP-15771). Branch `feature/tls-captured-effective-status` (PR #1108): original 3 commits `8d2ee5cdb`, `e5d0c65a1`, `237de66a9` off `b0f4decab`, then `4303e0f0f` (seed re-run fix), `a86cb662f` merge of develop (1.3.1), `47fc7db34` test adjustment, `04ac9885e` EPP-15598 doc alignment, `d359a44bd` review follow-ups; tip `d359a44bd`, merges clean. Facts that shaped it: **no status column exists** on either per-state table — `INIT` lives only in the stored JSON at `$.transactionRecord[0].transactionDetails.status`; the TIS contract has no status field (events carry state/substate/payload); correlation key = `(tenant_id, transaction_id)` (RPS `TransactionDetails.Ident` vs TDS `transactionId` header; scope_id excluded — RPS writes 0, TDS writes JWT scope); the existing authorized index has capture_date in the middle so a new `idx_authorized_txn_log_correlation (tenant_id, transaction_id)` was added. Solution: Liquibase 1.4.0 = view `captured_transaction_log_effective` (same columns; payload status rewritten to ACCEPTED via guarded plpgsql helpers only when an authorized row EXISTS; `effective_status` column) + index; RPS retrieve step + `message-flow-retrieve.yaml` and TIS `captured` routing point at the view; authorized/default untouched; OpenAPI untouched. Proof: new zonky+Liquibase DB test in `transaction-log-repository-db` (8 tests: full changelog applied twice, scenarios A–E, base row byte-for-byte unchanged, cross-tenant isolation, malformed payload safety, EXPLAIN shows index-only probe on the correlation index); binding-kit 262, common 6, TIS 353, collector 206 all green; e2e scenario + seed written (not executed); doc `core-services/transaction-log-repository/docs/captured-effective-status.md`. **Open question to raise with Vlad/Kumaran before merge:** equality of the RPS ident and the Base24-eps `transactionId` header, and tenant (RPS hard-codes Root; TDS leg tenant from JWT) — if they differ the view never matches and everything stays INIT. Build note: Nexus/VPN were down; built via an init script outside the repo (local-cache mirror, generateGitProperties disabled). **Done 2026-08-25:** develop fetched (`a3d7a8518`, 129 commits ahead of base, none touching TLRS/banking-utils/tlrs-e2e; merge clean, no rebase needed), branch pushed, **PR #1108 raised** (reviewers Vlad + Kumaran) with the evidence and the correlation-key open question in the description. Worktree removed. **Real-interface verification (Aug 25, local Docker stack built from the branch: postgres 15, Liquibase image, NATS, TLRS collector, TIS):** migration applied cleanly on a fresh DB (18 changesets, ends with the two 1.4.0 ones); **AC5** tlrs-e2e over NATS: @smoke (INIT) PASS, @effective-status (txn-004 → ACCEPTED) PASS, @multi-retrieve PASS; **AC4** TIS `GET /Transaction/e2e-retrieve-txn-004/captured` 200 with payload transactionDetails.status = ACCEPTED, txn-001 → INIT, POST find state eq 'captured' returns all four (summary projection); **AC3** base row still INIT; **AC8** EXPLAIN = Index Only Scan on the correlation index. Defect found and fixed on the branch (`4303e0f0f`): e2e seed cleanup did not remove the seeded authorized row → re-run failed on the authorized PK. Evidence posted as a comment on PR #1108. Environment findings (not this PR): dev compose sets AUTHZ_SKIP_SSL=true without SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE so TLS/TIS refuse to start; tlrs-db compose passes SPRING_DATASOURCE_* that the Liquibase image ignores; the internal base-image registry fails TLS trust from this Mac (built with a public Temurin base for the test); e2e needs BSI_XSD_ROOT and a Postgres port other than 5432 (host Postgres occupies it). Containers left running under compose project `tlsverify` (postgres :15432, nats, tlrs-service :8090, tis-service :8085; images tagged `:verify`). Story DoD now fully met except the correlation-key confirmation from a live environment. **Correlation check in banking-ep (Aug 26, SELECT-only via a throwaway psql pod against the external VM DB 10.86.117.39:5345/solmcasutr):** captured 38 rows, authorized 1815. The captured txn Supriya sent (`a01150417268d8434192938be77c7ee098a9`, Root, scope 0) has NO authorized row; matches on (tenant_id, transaction_id) = 0, on transaction_id alone = 0. BUT both tables use the same id format (`a011` + 32 hex) and tenant `Root`; authorized rows carry scope_id 1 (JWT) vs captured 0 (RPS) — confirms scope_id must stay out of the key. Timelines don't overlap: authorized rows stop 2026-08-14 (TDS/Base24-eps runs), captured rows are the RPS tests of 2026-08-19–24 → the two legs have only ever been exercised separately in banking-ep; no end-to-end transaction exists there yet. Conclusion: key is format- and tenant-compatible; proof of equality needs one transaction that runs both legs (RPS create + Base24-eps authorization) — ask the RPS/Vikesh side to run one in banking-ep, or use the cards-devops smoke round trip once TPS accept is fixed. Rule recorded: these VM databases are SELECT-only. **Decision (Narendra, Aug 26): option 2 — the correlation proof comes from the first cards-devops smoke round-trip transaction after PR #1067 lands; finding posted on PR #1108 as a comment; no further data ask to the RPS side.** **Aug 28 rework commit `f6fcd12fd` (new tip) — see §8 row.**

