## 11. Lessons and gotchas (things that cost time)

- Private AKS API is unreachable over VPN → use `az aks command invoke` (kubectl runs in Azure; `--file` uploads).
- Cluster webhook injects `HTTP_PROXY` into pods; busybox wget ignores `no_proxy` → `unset HTTP_PROXY http_proxy HTTPS_PROXY https_proxy` in any in-cluster script (the Testkube step does this).
- macOS `tar` adds `._*` resource-fork files that `bru` fails to parse → `COPYFILE_DISABLE=1 tar`.
- `/tmp` on macOS gets purged → keep evidence under `~/work/ga_evidence/`.
- Develop moved under the DM branch: ADR numbers 0031–0035 already taken; `cards-auth-interfaces` collection already copied; Dockerfile uses a Nexus `REGISTRY` arg — always build branches from `origin/develop`, not from the DM branch.
- Jira PATs expire/rotate; the account cannot create EPP issues.
- The API-Configuration importer rejects a changed `info.version` for in-place updates.
- Automated PR review produced one real finding (PR 1005 startup race) and one fabricated one (PR 993 "shared Dockerfile") — verify against the repo before acting.
- Microsoft Graph (Teams read) rate-limits hard; search endpoints are separate from chat-read.
- ADR numbers race: develop claimed 0036 the same day we picked it → check `git ls-tree origin/develop docs/adr/domain-services/` right before raising/merging.
- EPP tickets above ~13111 are on Jira Cloud; the server PAT and `ga_evidence/` only see the old backlog; Jira notification emails are the fallback for reading a ticket.
- A date bound on the captured→authorized correlation looked like the obvious fix for identifier reuse, but the two `capture_date` columns are on different clocks (RPS UTC processing date vs Base24-eps business date `captrDat`), so any bound silently turns authorized transactions into INIT-forever. When two legs are written by different systems, check what each column actually means before comparing them. (PR #1108, Aug 28; reverted same day.)
- Moving a guarded helper into `CROSS JOIN LATERAL` makes Postgres run it for every row even when the column is not projected; select-list expressions are dropped when unprojected and skipped by CASE. Keep per-row plpgsql in the select list.
- Time-filtered PR/Teams sweeps miss reviews that landed earlier in the day (Kumaran's #1108 review was missed by a "since last night" filter) — sweep by reviewer status, not by timestamp.
- Liquibase 1.3.1 enforces `UNIQUE (tenant_id, capture_date, transaction_id)`; any test fixture with same-day duplicates fails on develop now.
- TIS liveness is `/health/liveness` on port 9096 (not in the Service); `/actuator/health` on the app port is what the Service exposes and what the smoke uses.

